# Example htpasswd file for the backup-monitor Traefik basic-auth.
#
# DO NOT commit a real file named `backup-monitor-htpasswd` to git.
# It is generated per environment with a random password by
# scripts/setup/create-secrets.sh (generate_htpasswd_line "admin") and
# copied here at deploy time. If the real file is absent, Traefik refuses
# to serve the route (fail-closed) — that is the intended behaviour.
#
# Format (one "user:bcrypt-hash" line per user):
#   admin:$2y$05$REPLACED_WITH_A_RANDOM_BCRYPT_HASH
#
# To add a user manually:
#   htpasswd -B traefik-dynamic/backup-monitor-htpasswd <username>
